  "key_findings": [
    "Dataset covers 64,738 subscribers with a baseline 30-day churn rate of 1.73% (1,122 churned vs. 63,616 retained), an imbalance of roughly 1 churner per 57 retained subscribers.",
    "'Uttar Pradesh East' circle shows the highest churn concentration at 2.8%, making it the top-priority region for retention campaigns.",
    "Churn risk accelerates sharply once the recharge gap reaches the '90+'-day band, marking the 'silent churn' threshold for proactive outreach.",
    "The '<150' INR ARPU bracket has the highest churn rate at 3.2%, pointing to pricing/value-perception risk in that tier.",
    "'days_since_last_recharge' is the numeric feature most correlated with churn (r = 0.22), flagging it as a strong candidate signal for the predictive model."
